In `main()`, a developer writes:
```cpp
PcoThread t1(task1);
t1.join();
PcoThread t2(task2);
t2.join();
```
What is the execution behavior of `task1` and `task2`?

Consider:
```cpp
PcoThread *t1, *t2;
void f1() { t2->requestStop(); }
void f2() { while (!PcoThread::thisThread()->stopRequested()) {} }
int main() {
  t1 = new PcoThread(f1);
  t2 = new PcoThread(f2);
  t1->join(); t2->join();
}
```
Why can this program crash with a segmentation fault?
